# Trivy ignore list — CVEs triaged and accepted, not "unfixed" (ignore-unfixed
# already filters those). Re-evaluate whenever the bundled tool is bumped.
#
# lazydocker (Containerfile.toolbox-dev, LAZYDOCKER_VERSION) — v0.25.2 is the
# latest upstream release (github.com/jesseduffield/lazydocker) and is built
# against an older Go toolchain/vendored docker client, so trivy's gobinary
# scanner flags stdlib + vendored-dependency CVEs baked into that release.
# lazydocker is a local, interactive terminal UI talking to the local Docker
# socket inside a toolbox container — it does not act as a TLS/HTTP server or
# parse untrusted network input, so these DoS/parsing bugs are not reachable
# in how it's used here. No upstream fix exists yet; bump LAZYDOCKER_VERSION
# and drop the matching lines below once a release ships with patched deps.
CVE-2025-15558
CVE-2026-34040
CVE-2026-25679
CVE-2026-27145
CVE-2026-32280
CVE-2026-32281
CVE-2026-32283
CVE-2026-33811
CVE-2026-33814
CVE-2026-39820
CVE-2026-39836
CVE-2026-42499

# Pinned upstream release binaries (lazydocker in Containerfile.toolbox-dev;
# terraform/kubectl/flux/talosctl in Containerfile.toolbox-infra) — all
# installed as SHA256-verified upstream binaries, built by their own project
# against whatever Go toolchain/vendored deps they shipped with at release
# time. We don't control that build, only which pinned version we fetch.
# CVE-2026-39822 (Go stdlib os.Root symlink traversal) and CVE-2026-42504
# (Go net/mime DoS) are baked into every one of these binaries since they
# predate the patched Go point releases (1.25.11/1.25.12, 1.26.4/1.26.5).
# None of these tools run as a service accepting attacker-controlled
# filesystem paths or MIME input in how they're used here (interactive CLIs
# in a local toolbox talking to Docker/k8s/cloud APIs the user configures).
# CVE-2026-25681, CVE-2026-27136 and CVE-2026-39821 are golang.org/x/net
# (HTML parsing / Punycode/IDNA) CVEs vendored into kubectl — kubectl talks
# to the Kubernetes API over TLS/JSON, it does not parse attacker-supplied
# HTML or Punycode in normal use, so these are not reachable either.
# Re-evaluate and drop the matching lines below once each tool's
# *_VERSION is bumped to a release built with patched deps.
CVE-2026-39822
CVE-2026-42504
CVE-2026-25681
CVE-2026-27136
CVE-2026-39821
